/T (The commodities market is often split into two broad categories: hard and soft commodities. Hard commodities include natural resources that must be mined or extracted, such as gold, silver, rubber, and oil, whereas soft commodities are agricultural products or livestock, such as corn, wheat, coffee, and sugar. Typically, commodities allow traders to profit from price fluctuations and investors to diversify their portfolios and hedge against inflation.)
/E (The commodities market is often split into two broad categories: hard and soft commodities. Hard commodities include natural resources that must be mined or extracted, such as gold, silver, rubber, and oil, whereas soft commodities are agricultural products or livestock, such as corn, wheat, coffee, and sugar. Typically, commodities allow traders to profit from price fluctuations and investors to diversify their portfolios and hedge against inflation.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [1]
