/T (The basic economic principles of supply and demand drive commodities markets. Low supply and high demand equate to higher prices. High supply and low demand equate to lower prices. Therefore, factors such as currency fluctuations, geopolitical and economic stability, disruption in logistics and supply chains, global economic changes and developments, as well as technical changes can all influence the price action of commodities.)
/E (The basic economic principles of supply and demand drive commodities markets. Low supply and high demand equate to higher prices. High supply and low demand equate to lower prices. Therefore, factors such as currency fluctuations, geopolitical and economic stability, disruption in logistics and supply chains, global economic changes and developments, as well as technical changes can all influence the price action of commodities.)
