1495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 816 0 R
/E (Identifying trends is a fundamental aspect of technical analysis. Trends can be upward \(bullish\), downward \(bearish\), or sideways \(neutral\). Trends are identified by higher highs and higher lows, trading ranges, or lower highs and lower lows \(see image below\). Trends are often drawn to highlight the direction of price movement and then used to determine our daily bias, which is used to determine whether we look for long \(buy\) or short \(sell\) positions.)
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 816 0 R
/E (Trends and trend lines are used to help you understand market structure, which is the behavior, condition, and current flow of the market. Market structure can tell you if the market is trending or not so you can identify potential trade opportunities and make informed decisions based on the market direction.)
/Pg 60 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
