1635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 824 0 R
/E (Supply and demand zones are a popular analysis technique used in day trading. The zones are the periods of sideways price action that come before explosive price moves and are typically marked out using a rectangle tool on the chart. Supply and demand zones are similar to support and resistance, but the main difference is that support and resistance are levels or lines in which prices were already determined, while supply and demand are fresh levels or zones in which prices are not determined.)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
