/E (The regulatory environment plays a significant role in shaping Bitcoin's regulatory landscape. Government policies, tax treatment, and legal frameworks governing cryptocurrencies impact investor confidence, market liquidity, and institutional participation. Compliance with anti-money laundering \(AML\) and know-your-customer \(KYC\) regulations is crucial for Bitcoin exchanges and service providers, influencing market accessibility and investor trust.)
/Pg 79 0 R
