/P 855 0 R
/E (Impatient traders are always in pursuit of the next big trade. They jump into trades without a clear plan, hoping to catch quick profits. This impulsive behavior often leads to losses. Impatience, or "itchy feet" in trading, arises from a desire for instant gratification. In a society accustomed to immediate results, impatience may prompt you to enter positions early, without conducting proper research or analysis.)
/Pg 99 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1929 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 855 0 R
/E (The impatient trader also feels the need for constant action, which can lead to overtrading. Overtrading is where traders make numerous trades in a short period, often spreading themselves too thin and not thinking critically about their trade positions. While they may get lucky occasionally, trading without proper research or analysis typically leads to losses.)
/Pg 99 0 R
/K [6]
>>
