2044 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 867 0 R
/E (Forward testing is a method of evaluating the performance of a trading strategy by applying it to real-time market data and observing how it performs in real-time, on data that the strategy has not seen before. This is in contrast to backtesting, which involves applying a strategy to historical data and observing how it would have performed in the past. This practice bridges the gap between theory and live trading, offering a risk-free environment for refining your skills if conducted on a paper trading \(demo\) account. Here's how it works.)
/Pg 111 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
2045 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 867 0 R
/E (1. Implementing the Strategy: Execute trades based on the rules of your trading strategy and the results of your backtesting, just as you would in live trading. However, instead of using real money, you use a demo account provided by a trading platform.)
/Pg 111 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
2046 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 867 0 R
/E (2. Real-Time Market Conditions: Trades are executed in real-time, reflecting the current market prices and conditions. This allows you to gauge how your strategy performs in the actual market environment.)
/Pg 111 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2047 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 867 0 R
/E (3. Tracking Performance: Monitor the performance of your strategy during the forward testing period, keeping track of key metrics such as profitability, win rate, maximum drawdown, and risk-adjusted returns.)
/Pg 111 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
2048 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 867 0 R
/E (4. Learning and Adjustment: Forward testing provides valuable insights into how your trading strategy performs in practice. You can observe how the strategy reacts to different market scenarios and identify any weaknesses or areas for improvement.)
/Pg 111 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
2049 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 867 0 R
/E (5. Refinement and Optimization: Based on the results of forward testing, you should refine and optimize your trading strategy to enhance its performance. This may involve adjusting parameters, adding new rules, or fine-tuning risk management techniques.)
/Pg 111 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
2050 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 867 0 R
/E (6. Validation: Forward testing serves as a form of validation for the trading strategy. By testing the strategy in real-time market conditions, you gain confidence in its effectiveness and reliability.)
/Pg 111 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
2051 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 867 0 R
/E (104)
/Pg 111 0 R
/K [8]
