/E (Displacement is characterized by a sudden and forceful price movement, either upwards or downwards. On a price chart, it typically appears as a sequence of consecutive long candles with minimal wicks, all moving in the same direction.)
/Pg 123 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 879 0 R
/E (Two key points to remember about Displacement are that it often signifies a sudden surge in buying or selling pressure, frequently occurring when the price reaches a Liquidity level. Additionally, Displacement almost invariably results in two significant outcomes: a Market Structure Shift and a Fair Value Gap.)
/Pg 123 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
