/E (When a Liquidity level is breached and a trend reversal occurs, traders often observe a gap on their charts. This is referred to as a Fair Value Gap. Specifically, a Fair Value Gap consists of three candles, with a larger one at the center and a gap between its wicks and those of the surrounding candles. Fair Value Gaps tend to be filled at some point in the future, and this is the concept that traders leverage when setting their orders.)
/Pg 126 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
